sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User or Upstream System
    participant A as AI Agent
    participant I as Identity and Authority Service
    participant P as Policy and Risk Engine
    participant H as Human Approval Service
    participant C as Capability Broker
    participant R as Controlled Runtime
    participant T as Tool or Connector
    participant E as Evidence and Audit Layer
    participant M as Monitoring and Response

    U->>A: Submit request
    A->>E: Record request origin and intent
    A->>I: Validate identity, role, and delegated authority

    alt Identity or authority cannot be verified
        I-->>A: Deny
        A->>E: Record denial reason
        A-->>U: Refuse or escalate
    else Identity and authority verified
        I-->>A: Verified trust context
        A->>P: Submit structured action request
        P->>E: Record policy inputs and evaluation

        alt Policy denies action
            P-->>A: Deny
            A->>E: Record policy denial
            A-->>U: Refuse request
        else Additional approval required
            P-->>A: Approval required
            A->>H: Request scoped approval
            H->>E: Record approval decision

            alt Approval denied or expired
                H-->>A: Deny
                A-->>U: Refuse or request revised scope
            else Approval granted
                H-->>A: Approved scope and validity
                A->>C: Request constrained capability
            end
        else Policy allows with constraints
            P-->>A: Allowed scope and constraints
            A->>C: Request constrained capability
        end

        C->>E: Record issued capability and limits
        C-->>R: Issue time-limited, least-privilege capability
        R->>E: Record execution start
        R->>T: Invoke approved action
        T-->>R: Return result or error
        R->>E: Record result, status, and integrity metadata
        R->>M: Emit telemetry and security events

        alt Anomaly or policy violation detected
            M->>C: Revoke or suspend capability
            M->>R: Contain, cancel, or isolate execution
            M->>E: Record incident and containment actions
            R-->>A: Execution contained
            A-->>U: Report controlled failure or escalation
        else Execution completes within constraints
            M->>E: Record normal completion telemetry
            R-->>A: Return verified result
            A-->>U: Deliver result
        end
    end
